om/story/mack-mygarage-lets-customers-save-customize-truck-builds-4e1021998a/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 18:55:25 +0000</pubDate><category>Equipment</category><description>Truck News</description></item><item><title>EV Realty breaks ground on 9 MW truck charging hub in California</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/ev-realty-breaks-ground-on-9-mw-truck-charging-hub-in-california-43312477df/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/ev-realty-breaks-ground-on-9-mw-truck-charging-hub-in-california-43312477df/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 18:55:22 +0000</pubDate><category>Equipment</category><description>Truck News</description></item><item><title>Broker RXO says TL spot rates not entering deflationary phase</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/broker-rxo-says-tl-spot-rates-not-entering-deflationary-phase-a17334730a/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/broker-rxo-says-tl-spot-rates-not-entering-deflationary-phase-a17334730a/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 17:13:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Rates &amp; Market</category><description>FreightWaves</description></item><item><title>CBSA officers seize 81 kg of suspected cocaine from a commercial truck arriving from the US, at Pacific Highway</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/cbsa-officers-seize-81-kg-of-suspected-cocaine-from-a-commercial-truck-d57d869691/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/cbsa-officers-seize-81-kg-of-suspected-cocaine-from-a-commercial-truck-d57d869691/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 17:00:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Cross-Border</category><description>Canada Border Services Agency</description></item><item><title>Q3 2026 Cargo Theft Falls as Losses Rise</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/q3-2026-cargo-theft-falls-as-losses-rise-036656251d/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/q3-2026-cargo-theft-falls-as-losses-rise-036656251d/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 16:55:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Verisk CargoNet reported 547 supply chain crime incidents involving cargo across the U.S. and Canada in the third quarter of 2026, down 33% from a year earlier and 19% from the second quarter. Estimated losses still rose 12% to $230.1 million. Fictitious pickups, in which criminals use deception to obtain a shipment, fell only 6% to 138, so their share of reported activity rose to about 25%.

Through September, reported incidents were down 25% year to date, while estimated losses rose 39% to $718.9 million. The average value of stolen goods with a documented value rose 72% to $448,456. CargoNet logged 19 thefts of $1 million or more, compared with nine a year earlier. California accounted for about a third of incidents, and four states made up 57% of the quarterly total. CargoNet also documented fraud schemes in 2026 that used compromised email accounts, internet phone systems and transportation applications, and said theft has historically risen in Q4.</description></item><item><title>Cass Freight Index: Freight cycle finds a higher gear</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/cass-freight-index-freight-cycle-finds-a-higher-gear-06303619b7/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/cass-freight-index-freight-cycle-finds-a-higher-gear-06303619b7/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 16:49:43 +0000</pubDate><category>Rates &amp; Market</category><description>TheTrucker.com</description></item><item><title>The Right Tool for the Job: The Reality of AI in Freight</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/the-right-tool-for-the-job-the-reality-of-ai-in-freight-e333eb61f7/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/the-right-tool-for-the-job-the-reality-of-ai-in-freight-e333eb61f7/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 16:48:41 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Transport Topics</description></item><item><title>Petro-Canada PC-12 Engine Oils: What Fleets Need to Know for 2027</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/petro-canada-pc-12-engine-oils-what-fleets-need-to-know-for-2027-196e2beda6/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/petro-canada-pc-12-engine-oils-what-fleets-need-to-know-for-2027-196e2beda6/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 16:40:13 +0000</pubDate><category>Equipment</category><description>Commercial Carrier Journal</description></item><item><title>Saia asks FMCSA to allow CLP holders to operate CMVs with double trailers under supervision</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/saia-asks-fmcsa-to-allow-clp-holders-to-operate-cmvs-with-double-trail-0abe1c2af4/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/saia-asks-fmcsa-to-allow-clp-holders-to-operate-cmvs-with-double-trail-0abe1c2af4/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 16:30:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Regulations</category><description>CDLLife</description></item><item><title>SONAR Pricing Power Index Falls to 68 as Truckload Demand Weakens</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/sonar-pricing-power-index-falls-to-68-as-truckload-demand-weakens-f7a5bc99cc/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/sonar-pricing-power-index-falls-to-68-as-truckload-demand-weakens-f7a5bc99cc/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 15:59:57 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>FreightWaves</description></item><item><title>Oil market slide brings benchmark diesel under $6 level</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/oil-market-slide-brings-benchmark-diesel-under-6-level-daba6fe391/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/oil-market-slide-brings-benchmark-diesel-under-6-level-daba6fe391/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 15:50:51 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>FreightWaves</description></item><item><title>Diesel prices fall to under $6 per gallon</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/diesel-prices-fall-to-under-6-per-gallon-b8de84d4b1/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/diesel-prices-fall-to-under-6-per-gallon-b8de84d4b1/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 15:46:58 +0000</pubDate><category>Fuel</category><description>The national average diesel price fell 19 cents per gallon, from $6.127 to $5.937, according to the weekly report from the United States Energy Information Agency. Every reporting region dropped by double digits. The Central Atlantic had the smallest decline, from $6.412 to $6.309, while the Midwest had the largest, from $6.201 to $5.967. The article links the drop to slipping oil prices. On an early Tuesday, the Associated Press reported that Brent crude edged 49 cents lower to $92.93 a barrel and U.S. benchmark crude slid 51 cents to $86.23 per barrel.</description></item><item><title>New specific bonus for fuel tanker truck drivers</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/new-specific-bonus-for-fuel-tanker-truck-drivers-379f9abb9a/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/new-specific-bonus-for-fuel-tanker-truck-drivers-379f9abb9a/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 14:22:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Equipment</category><description>Nessma TV</description></item><item><title>Truck Parking Club hands CPC 7 drop yards in two months</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/truck-parking-club-hands-cpc-7-drop-yards-in-two-months-ac60a533be/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/truck-parking-club-hands-cpc-7-drop-yards-in-two-months-ac60a533be/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 14:18:46 +0000</pubDate><category>Drivers &amp; Jobs</category><description>FreightWaves</description></item><item><title>Six commercial vehicles placed out of service in Ontario during enforcement blitz</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/six-commercial-vehicles-placed-out-of-service-in-ontario-during-enforc-9f6c87c542/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/six-commercial-vehicles-placed-out-of-service-in-ontario-during-enforc-9f6c87c542/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 14:14:57 +0000</pubDate><category>Regulations</category><description>Truck News</description></item><item><title>Shippers Are Finally Ready to Fix the Supply Chain Behind the Freight Bill</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/shippers-are-finally-ready-to-fix-the-supply-chain-behind-the-freight-f5ed5bdb3f/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/shippers-are-finally-ready-to-fix-the-supply-chain-behind-the-freight-f5ed5bdb3f/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 14:05:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Regulations</category><description>FreightWaves</description></item><item><title>Manitoba trucking industry celebrates heroism and service</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/manitoba-trucking-industry-celebrates-heroism-and-service-cc704ee782/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/manitoba-trucking-industry-celebrates-heroism-and-service-cc704ee782/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 14:04:26 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Truck News</description></item><item><title>FleetWatcher adds driver certification tracking</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/fleetwatcher-adds-driver-certification-tracking-4f383b61e4/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/fleetwatcher-adds-driver-certification-tracking-4f383b61e4/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 13:59:18 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Truck News</description></item><item><title>Five Manitoba fleets join Trucking HR Canada’s Women’s Leadership Accord</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/five-manitoba-fleets-join-trucking-hr-canada-s-women-s-leadership-acco-1571d7c228/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/five-manitoba-fleets-join-trucking-hr-canada-s-women-s-leadership-acco-1571d7c228/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 13:45:36 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Truck News</description></item><item><title>Man, 24, dies in head-on crash between semi-trailer and truck in Manitoba&#x27;s Interlake</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/man-24-dies-in-head-on-crash-between-semi-trailer-and-truck-in-manitob-3a17264ddd/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/man-24-dies-in-head-on-crash-between-semi-trailer-and-truck-in-manitob-3a17264ddd/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 13:41:37 +0000</pubDate><category>Equipment</category><description>CBC</description></item><item><title>GTCC and Old Dominion Freight Line support future truckers</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/gtcc-and-old-dominion-freight-line-support-future-truckers-27332026fc/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/gtcc-and-old-dominion-freight-line-support-future-truckers-27332026fc/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 13:19:18 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Guilford Technical Community College in Greensboro runs a truck driver training program that staff say has grown every year since it started six years ago. The certificate takes eight weeks of full-time study or 14 weeks of nights and weekends, and costs about $1,800 including books. Jan Knox, VP of the college advancement foundation, said graduates can often find work right away at a salary of $60,000 or more.

Old Dominion Freight Line, a trucking company headquartered in the Triad, is funding four $1,000 scholarships a year at the college, two of them for women. Chris Brooks, Senior VP of HR at the company, said the awards help people who might not otherwise afford a CDL or a diesel mechanic certification. The company said it has over 200 women drivers.</description></item><item><title>Truckload Carriers Association Outlines FMCSA Reform Strategy</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/truckload-carriers-association-outlines-fmcsa-reform-strategy-2a2b102a25/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/truckload-carriers-association-outlines-fmcsa-reform-strategy-2a2b102a25/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 12:43:07 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Commercial Carrier Journal</description></item><item><title>US cargo theft falls 8% in Q3 as truck stop incidents nearly triple</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/us-cargo-theft-falls-8-in-q3-as-truck-stop-incidents-nearly-triple-bdd1f4a40c/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/us-cargo-theft-falls-8-in-q3-as-truck-stop-incidents-nearly-triple-bdd1f4a40c/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 11:59:24 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Truck News</description></item><item><title>The &quot;Mighty Mitch&quot; Method: Logistics Growth, Tech, &amp; People — What The Truck?!?</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/the-mighty-mitch-method-logistics-growth-tech-people-what-the-truck-9d4c887eb0/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/the-mighty-mitch-method-logistics-growth-tech-people-what-the-truck-9d4c887eb0/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 11:19:09 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>FreightWaves</description></item><item><title>Should Truck Drivers Have an Age Limit? The I-84 Rollover Debate — What The Truck?!?</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/should-truck-drivers-have-an-age-limit-the-i-84-rollover-debate-what-t-9b7c99251f/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/should-truck-drivers-have-an-age-limit-the-i-84-rollover-debate-what-t-9b7c99251f/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 09:51:09 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>FreightWaves</description></item><item><title>Shift Supervisor - Logistics in Minneapolis, MN for Penske Truck Leasing</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/shift-supervisor-logistics-in-minneapolis-mn-for-penske-truck-leasing-55ca7af8e1/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/shift-supervisor-logistics-in-minneapolis-mn-for-penske-truck-leasing-55ca7af8e1/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 09:10:50 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Transport Topics</description></item><item><title>Higher diesel prices strain farm transportation budgets</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/higher-diesel-prices-strain-farm-transportation-budgets-e7952ede0c/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/higher-diesel-prices-strain-farm-transportation-budgets-e7952ede0c/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 08:02:23 +0000</pubDate><category>Fuel</category><description>Higher diesel prices are adding costs for Iowa farmers and trucking operators, according to Matt Wells, vice president of the Mid-West Truckers Association. Wells cited refinery shutdowns, declining fuel reserves and the war between Russia and Ukraine as factors tightening supply. He said two California refineries were shut down and a refinery in Joliet, Illinois, was offline for seven to ten days, while Ukrainian attacks damaged Russian refining facilities.

Wells said transportation rates and operating budgets will need to reflect the higher costs, potentially for the next year to year and a half, and he does not expect diesel prices to fall significantly soon. He also cautioned that fuel prices do not always return to earlier levels after a large increase. On red-dyed diesel, Wells said the modern dyed product is essentially the same fuel as clear highway diesel, and that its use on public roads remains subject to federal and state tax requirements and any specifically authorized exemptions.</description></item><item><title>Detroit Diesel Promises 2027 Engines With No Penalties, 3% TCO Savings</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/detroit-diesel-promises-2027-engines-with-no-penalties-3-tco-savings-27e3bb0783/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/detroit-diesel-promises-2027-engines-with-no-penalties-3-tco-savings-27e3bb0783/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:44:02 +0000</pubDate><category>Equipment</category><description>Commercial Carrier Journal</description></item><item><title>Cybersecurity Training for Fleets, AI Logistics Tools &amp; more</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/cybersecurity-training-for-fleets-ai-logistics-tools-more-aca4446e8b/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/cybersecurity-training-for-fleets-ai-logistics-tools-more-aca4446e8b/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 23:48:56 +0000</pubDate><category>Drivers &amp; Jobs</category><description>Commercial Carrier Journal</description></item><item><title>How ATA Wants to Fix ELD Certification</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/how-ata-wants-to-fix-eld-certification-a812fcb144/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/how-ata-wants-to-fix-eld-certification-a812fcb144/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 22:51:16 +0000</pubDate><category>Regulations</category><description>Heavy Duty Trucking</description></item><item><title>New York defeats FMCSA in major legal battle over non-domicil